        <item rdf:about="https://www.nature.com/articles/s41567-026-03339-8">
            <title>[9] Microscopic signatures of an imaginary charge density wave in a kagome metal</title>
            <link>https://www.nature.com/articles/s41567-026-03339-8</link>
            <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><b>Last authors:</b> H. Kontani, Y. Matsuda</p><p><b>Authors:</b> S. Suetsugu, F. Hori, M. Shibata, et al.</p><p><span style='display:inline-block;padding:4px 9px;border-radius:999px;background:#fee2e2;color:#991b1b;font-weight:700;'>Score 9/10</span> <b>A_MUST_READ</b></p><p><b>Why:</b> title strong match: kagome metal</p><p><b>Tags:</b> <span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'>#kagome</span> <span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'>#CsV3Sb5</span> <span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'>#V3Sb5</span> <span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'>#chargedensitywave</span> <span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'>#loopcurrent</span> <span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'>#time-reversalsymmetrybreaking</span></p><p><img src='https://media.springernature.com/m685/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41567-026-03339-8/MediaObjects/41567_2026_3339_Fig1_HTML.png' style='max-width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:10px;' /></p><hr/><p><b>Abstract:</b> Nature Physics, Published online: 17 June 2026; doi:10.1038/s41567-026-03339-8 Whether imaginary charge density waves and their associated loop currents exist has remained an open question. Now signatures of this state have been observed in kagome metal CsV3Sb5, revealing spontaneous time-reversal symmetry breaking.</p>]]></content:encoded>
            <dc:title>[9] Microscopic signatures of an imaginary charge density wave in a kagome metal</dc:title>
            <dc:creator>Last authors: H. Kontani, Y. Matsuda; Authors: S. Suetsugu, F. Hori, M. Shibata, et al.</dc:creator><dc:creator>F. Hori</dc:creator><dc:creator>M. Shibata</dc:creator><dc:creator>S. Kitagawa</dc:creator><dc:creator>K. Ishida</dc:creator><dc:creator>T. Asaba</dc:creator><dc:creator>S. Nakazawa</dc:creator><dc:creator>Q. Li</dc:creator><dc:creator>H. -H. Wen</dc:creator><dc:creator>T. Shibauchi</dc:creator><dc:creator>H. Kontani</dc:creator><dc:creator>Y. Matsuda</dc:creator>
            <dc:identifier>doi:10.1038/s41567-026-03339-8</dc:identifier>
            <dc:source>Nature Physics, Published online: 2026-06-17; | doi:10.1038/s41567-026-03339-8</dc:source>
            <dc:date>2026-06-17</dc:date>
            <prism:publicationName>Nature Physics</prism:publicationName>
            <prism:doi>10.1038/s41567-026-03339-8</prism:doi>
            <prism:url>https://www.nature.com/articles/s41567-026-03339-8</prism:url>
        <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Last authors:&lt;/b&gt; H. Kontani, Y. Matsuda&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Authors:&lt;/b&gt; S. Suetsugu, F. Hori, M. Shibata, et al.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style='display:inline-block;padding:4px 9px;border-radius:999px;background:#fee2e2;color:#991b1b;font-weight:700;'&gt;Score 9/10&lt;/span&gt; &lt;b&gt;A_MUST_READ&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Why:&lt;/b&gt; title strong match: kagome metal&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Tags:&lt;/b&gt; &lt;span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'&gt;#kagome&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'&gt;#CsV3Sb5&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'&gt;#V3Sb5&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'&gt;#chargedensitywave&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'&gt;#loopcurrent&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'&gt;#time-reversalsymmetrybreaking&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src='https://media.springernature.com/m685/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41567-026-03339-8/MediaObjects/41567_2026_3339_Fig1_HTML.png' style='max-width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:10px;' /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr/&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Abstract:&lt;/b&gt; Nature Physics, Published online: 17 June 2026; doi:10.1038/s41567-026-03339-8 Whether imaginary charge density waves and their associated loop currents exist has remained an open question. Now signatures of this state have been observed in kagome metal CsV3Sb5, revealing spontaneous time-reversal symmetry breaking.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item>
    
        <item rdf:about="https://www.nature.com/articles/s41567-026-03351-y">
